worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_installation_and_software_followups.js"
  ceiling 840
  rationale "Installation-guide conversion to scripts, software project follow-ups, JavaScript execution and the coding oracle with its write-program templates. Issue #658 cut this module out of one oversized worker file by line count; R1188-U5 named it after what it holds. Its ceiling falls as its logic moves into js/wasm-worker. The +18 lines over the previous 1198 ceiling are pure catalog data, not logic: hive-mind#2158 dispatched Hello World issues in Scala and Kotlin that no catalog language could answer, so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained scala and kotlin in Rust and this mirror gained the matching WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus their two hello_world templates. Mirroring only hello_world follows the existing sparse-coverage precedent (count_to_three carries 6 of 12 languages) and keeps every consumer of WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES consistent; the remaining task templates degrade through the blueprint and oracle fallbacks. The next +19 lines are the same kind of growth for the same reason: issue #1021 asked that a Russian request for PHP code (issue #723) be answered by generalization rather than by a rule written for its wording, and the generalization is cataloguing PHP the way Kotlin was catalogued -- so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained php in Rust and this mirror gained its WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus a php template in each of the task tables it already carries. Data, not logic: the mirror learned no new rule, only one more column of the table it already had. The next +16 lines are catalog data of the same kind, for the reason the PHP row did not settle: answering a request for Laravel in PHP answers the language the framework is written in, not the thing that was asked for (issue #723). The generalization widens the axis rather than adding a rule -- a row is an implementation target and a target may be a framework of another target -- so PROGRAM_LANGUAGES gained a laravel row in Rust and this mirror gained the matching WRITE_PROGRAM_LANGUAGES metadata plus its hello_world template. Without the mirror the browser engine would answer a bare Laravel request with nothing at all, because the surface moved out of the php meaning and into its own: the +16 lines are what keeps the mirror from regressing while the Rust engine improves. This data moves to js/wasm-worker with the rest of the write-program surface. Ceiling lowered 1251 to 1250 (2026-10-07, issue #1165 R1165-4): the rust, go and kotlin hello_world templates left WRITE_PROGRAM_TEMPLATES, because writeProgramTemplate rediscovers them from data/seed/coding-documentation-captures.lino. Ceiling lowered 1250 to 918 (2026-10-08, issue #921 R921-8): WRITE_PROGRAM_TASKS and WRITE_PROGRAM_TEMPLATES left this module entirely; installSeedProgramTasks fills both from data/seed/hello-world-programs.lino, so the worker answers every task in every language the Rust catalog holds (the Scala and Kotlin rows the sparse tables lacked included). Lowered 918 to 840 (2026-10-08, issue #918 installation_conversion migration): classifyInstallationVerb reads the installation_verb_action table and every installation sentence, step description and default project name is a seeded installation_* response."
